{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"scathing-washable-sapsucker","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# `plan_review/attest.py` is at the hard cap with ZERO headroom\n\n## Context\n\nLanding bug c083 (untracked-tolerance on four plan-review snapshot reads) hit this immediately: `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py` was **799** lines on `origin/main` against the **800** hard cap enforced by `tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py::test_no_src_module_over_the_hard_cap` (limit single-sourced in `.github/module-size-limit.txt`).\n\nA two-call-site change — adding `ignore_untracked=True` to two existing calls — could not be landed in the natural form:\n\n- appending the kwarg inline made the line 114 chars, over the ruff E501 limit of 100;\n- wrapping the call to satisfy E501 cost +2 lines -> 801, over the cap;\n- adding the explanatory comments the change deserved cost more -> 803.\n\nIt only fit by importing `collect_plan_relation_snapshot` directly (+1 line for the import, which let the call fit on one line at 95 chars), landing the file at **exactly 800** — passing only because the gate is `> limit`, with **zero** remaining headroom.\n\n## Why this is worth a ticket rather than a shrug\n\nThe next change to this file — any change, including a one-line bug fix — cannot land without first splitting it. The cost is not paid by whoever grew the file; it is paid by whoever next needs to fix a bug in it, under time pressure, as an unrelated blocker. That is exactly the situation task `2682` was raised for when `runner.py` hit 800 in the LLM-provider-seam epic, and it was resolved there by a real call-graph split (`runner.py` 800 -> 655 + `structured_run.py`).\n\nIt also actively degrades the code: in c083 the comments explaining WHY untracked files must be tolerated had to be cut from `attest.py` and replaced with a pointer to `resign.py`, purely to save lines. The cap is now shaping documentation quality, not just structure.\n\n## Approach\n\nSplit along a seam that ALREADY EXISTS in the call graph, per the module-size policy — never mechanically to hit a number, and never creating a sub-100-LOC file. Candidate seams to evaluate (not a decision):\n\n- the `refresh_attestation` / drift-refresh cluster (`_sidecar_branch_decision`, `refresh_attestation`, `_rehash`, `drift_refresh_candidate`) looks like a cohesive group distinct from the `sign_plan_review` path;\n- the manifest field/scope helpers (`_manifest_field`, `manifest_file_scope`, `_inherited_child_impact`).\n\nRequires the same seam analysis `2682` did: confirm the callers, keep reference sites resolving (watch string-literal monkeypatch targets in tests), and verify the split is import-cycle safe.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/attest.py` is under 700 LOC (real headroom, not 799)\n- [ ] any extracted module is at least 100 LOC (no sub-100-LOC fragmentation)\n- [ ] zero test edits are required by the move, or each required edit is justified in the commit message\n- [ ] the full suite passes with the same test count as before the split, plus any new seam tests","id":"c6c9-cba0-1aa4-47eb","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"task","title":"attest.py sits at exactly 800/800 LOC — zero headroom blocks the next edit"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785446529373002001,"uuid":"127618b6-2582-4981-8a8a-9926e38206b6"}